// Static behavioral API documentation for the BloodRoute backend.
// The document is a literal — it reads no actor state — so this mixin takes no
// parameters and declares exactly one method.
mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    let doc = "\n# BloodRoute Backend API\n\nBloodRoute plans blood-delivery routes from a patient/origin location to a\nhospital that holds the requested blood group, and lets a signed-in user save\nand track those requests.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\n- The app's frontend signs users in with Internet Identity and pins a\n  derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when\n  available. An agent that already holds the user's Internet Identity\n  authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin\n  (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation\n  acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- Registration is a prerequisite for the role-guarded methods. A direct API\n  caller must call `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in\n  (non-anonymous) caller before any role-guarded call, including the guarded\n  queries `getCallerUserRole` and `isCallerAdmin`. The first principal to\n  initialize becomes `#admin`; every later principal becomes `#user`. An\n  anonymous caller is ignored by initialization and reads as `#guest`.\n- A caller can be unregistered even when the app already knows it: registration\n  happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend, so a\n  principal that never did so is unregistered even if it belongs to the app's\n  owner. A signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different\n  principal than the one the frontend registered.\n- `getCallerUserRole` traps with `User is not registered` for a signed-in but\n  unregistered caller, and returns `#guest` for an anonymous caller.\n  `isCallerAdmin` traps the same way for an unregistered caller.\n- `assignCallerUserRole` traps with `Unauthorized: Only admins can assign user\n  roles` unless the caller is an admin.\n- The domain methods (`listHospitals`, `getHospital`, `searchHospitals`,\n  `upsertHospital`, `deleteHospital`, `computeRoute`, `listRequests`,\n  `getRequest`, `createRequest`, `updateRequestStatus`, `deleteRequest`,\n  `getProfile`, `setProfile`) do not check roles. They are callable by any\n  caller, including anonymous.\n\n## Hospitals\n\n- `listHospitals() : [Hospital]` — all hospitals.\n- `getHospital(id : Text) : ?Hospital` — one hospital by id, `null` if absent.\n- `searchHospitals(term : Text) : [Hospital]` — case-insensitive substring match\n  on `name` or `address`.\n- `upsertHospital(input : HospitalInput) : ()` — insert or replace by `id`.\n- `deleteHospital(id : Text) : ()` — remove by `id`; a no-op if absent.\n\n`Hospital` is `{ id : Text; name : Text; address : Text; lat : Float;\nlng : Float; stock : [BloodStock] }` and `BloodStock` is\n`{ bloodGroup : BloodGroup; units : Nat }`. `lat`/`lng` are decimal degrees.\n`stock` is a list of per-group unit counts; a group absent from the list counts\nas 0 units.\n\n## Blood groups and statuses\n\n`BloodGroup` is one of `#APos`, `#ANeg`, `#BPos`, `#BNeg`, `#ABPos`, `#ABNeg`,\n`#OPos`, `#ONeg`. `RequestStatus` is one of `#Pending`, `#InTransit`,\n`#Delivered`.\n\n## Route computation\n\n`computeRoute(request : RouteRequest) : RouteResult` is an **update** call\nbecause it performs an outbound HTTP request.\n\n`RouteRequest` is `{ originId : Text; originName : Text; originLat : Float;\noriginLng : Float; hospitalId : Text; bloodGroup : BloodGroup; units : Nat }`.\n`originId` and `originName` are carried for the caller's convenience and are not\nused in the computation.\n\n`RouteResult` is `{ distanceMeters : Nat; durationSeconds : Nat; geometry :\nText; originLat : Float; originLng : Float; destLat : Float; destLng : Float;\nbloodGroup : BloodGroup; units : Nat; stockSufficient : Bool; availableUnits :\nNat }`.\n\n- `distanceMeters` is whole meters; `durationSeconds` is whole seconds.\n- `geometry` is an OSRM polyline string, or `\"\"` when the fallback was used.\n- `stockSufficient` is `availableUnits >= units`, where `availableUnits` is the\n  hospital's stock for the requested `bloodGroup`.\n- **OSRM outcall fallback:** the route is fetched from the public OSRM driving\n  service. If that outcall fails or its response cannot be parsed, the backend\n  falls back to a straight-line (haversine) distance and returns\n  `durationSeconds = 0` and `geometry = \"\"`. A result is therefore always\n  produced for a known hospital; `durationSeconds = 0` with empty `geometry`\n  signals the fallback.\n- `computeRoute` traps with `Hospital not found: <id>` when `hospitalId` does\n  not exist.\n\n## Requests\n\n- `listRequests() : [BloodRequest]` — all saved requests.\n- `getRequest(id : Nat) : ?BloodRequest` — one request by id.\n- `createRequest(input : BloodRequestInput) : Nat` — saves a request and\n  returns its new id.\n- `updateRequestStatus(id : Nat, status : RequestStatus) : ()` — sets the\n  status and refreshes `updatedAt`. A no-op if the id is absent.\n- `deleteRequest(id : Nat) : ()` — removes by id; a no-op if absent.\n\n`BloodRequest` is `{ id : Nat; originName : Text; originLat : Float; originLng :\nFloat; hospitalId : Text; hospitalName : Text; bloodGroup : BloodGroup; units :\nNat; distanceMeters : Nat; durationSeconds : Nat; geometry : Text; status :\nRequestStatus; createdAt : Timestamp; updatedAt : Timestamp }`.\n`BloodRequestInput` omits `id`, `status`, `createdAt`, and `updatedAt`.\n\n- **Auto-increment ids:** `createRequest` assigns ids from a monotonic counter\n  starting at 0. Ids are never reused, including after `deleteRequest`.\n- `createRequest` always sets `status = #Pending` and `createdAt = updatedAt =\n  Time.now()` (nanoseconds since the Unix epoch). The caller supplies the route\n  fields; the backend does not recompute them.\n- `updateRequestStatus` sets `updatedAt = Time.now()` and leaves `createdAt`\n  unchanged.\n\n## Profiles\n\n- `getProfile() : ?Profile` — the caller's profile, `null` if unset.\n- `setProfile(displayName : Text, organizationName : Text) : ()` — upserts the\n  caller's profile.\n\n`Profile` is `{ displayName : Text; organizationName : Text }`. Profiles are\nkeyed by the caller's principal, so each principal has exactly one profile.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- `Timestamp` is `Nat` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch.\n- `units` is a count of blood bags.\n- `lat`/`lng` are decimal degrees as `Float`.\n- `distanceMeters` is meters, `durationSeconds` is seconds.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `upsertHospital`, `setProfile`, and `updateRequestStatus` are idempotent for\n  the same arguments.\n- `createRequest` is **not** idempotent: each call allocates a new id and\n  inserts a new row. Retrying a timed-out `createRequest` can create a\n  duplicate.\n- `deleteHospital` and `deleteRequest` are idempotent.\n\n## Errors and limits\n\n- `computeRoute` traps on an unknown hospital.\n- `getCallerUserRole` and `isCallerAdmin` trap for an unregistered signed-in\n  caller.\n- `assignCallerUserRole` traps for a non-admin caller.\n- `computeRoute` depends on an external routing service; expect the haversine\n  fallback when it is unavailable.\n\n## OQL data access\n\nThe canister exposes `schema()` and `execute()` through the Caffeine OQL\n`Expose` mixin. The queryable entities are `hospital`, `request`, and\n`profile`, all registered as public (any caller, including anonymous, may\nread). `execute()` accepts a JSON query and returns JSON rows.\n";
    doc;
  };
};
